7
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:59,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Today, as we scrutinize the proposed 2027 budget of the Department of Budget and Management and the special purpose funds, we do so in light of the recent landmark decision of the Supreme Court concerning the constitutionality of certain provisions under previous and present General Appropriations Acts. Bagamat hindi dineklara ng Supreme Court na unconstitutional ang unprogrammed appropriations, malinaw ang naging paalala nito sa Kongreso. We have a constitutional duty to exercise fiscal discipline,

8
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:29,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: uphold transparency and accountability, and ensure that every appropriation complies with the mandates of our Constitution. Malinaw po sa inyong lingkod at sa committee na ito ang ating tungkulin. We must ensure that the national budget is not only fiscally sound and responsive to the needs of our people, but also fully compliant with the Constitution. In its decision, the Supreme Court reminded us

9
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:59,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of the fundamental responsibility that comes with the power of the purse. Every peso collected in taxes and fees represents labor rendered, needs deferred, perseverance and sacrifice endured by our people. The General Appropriations Act [unclear] that sacrifice. This should guide us throughout our deliberations and remind us that the power of appropriations is not without limits, especially in light of the provisions provided in the 1987 Constitution.

10
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:29,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya naman po mahalaga ang papel ng DBM sa landmark desisyon na ito. Bukod sa 2.9 bilyon na pondo ng ahensya, ang DBM ay responsable din sa management ng higit-kumulang 550 billion na special purpose funds at unprogrammed appropriations. Nais nating malaman ngayong araw: una, ano ang implikasyon ng desisyon ng Korte Suprema sa binabalangkas nating national budget para sa Fiscal Year 2027?

11
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:59,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pangalawa, anong adjustments ang kailangan nating baguhin sa kasalukuyang version ng budget upang maiwasan ang anumang constitutional infirmities? Our responsibility does not end with determining how much the government may spend. We must also ensure that public funds are appropriated for clearly defined purposes, supported by available resources, and subject to proper safeguards and accountability.

12
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:29,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa madaling salita, hindi sapat na may pondong inilaan. Kailangan malinaw kung saan ito gagamitin, paano ito popondohan, sino ang makikinabang, at paano natin matitiyak na ito ay magagamit nang tama at wasto. At the start of our budget deliberations in the Senate, this representation emphasized our commitment to passing a national budget that responds to the basic needs of our people. Today, as we conduct the last day of budget briefing before sponsoring the proposed

13
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:59,980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 2027 national budget, allow me to reaffirm that commitment and underscore an equally important responsibility: to ensure that the budget we pass can stand constitutional scrutiny, reflects sound fiscal management, and delivers meaningful and tangible benefits to the Filipino people. Thank you very much. At this point, the Chair would like to acknowledge Senator Marcos for her opening statement.

